    <time>1788270431</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to a pinned upstream master snapshot, 0.3.4+git20251009.143ff5e
(143ff5e7e0f786e341df8846c04e8273c5183c26, 2025-10-09).

Supersedes sr#1374754, which carried only the Requires change below.

The 0.3.4 tag is from 2022-01; master is 7 commits ahead of it and all of
them are bug fixes:

- setBandwidth stored the request rounded through
  hackrf_compute_baseband_filter_bw, and setSampleRate then overrode it
  again whenever auto-bandwidth was on. Both are gone, so a requested
  bandwidth now survives a sample-rate change.
- hackrf_set_amp_enable() was only called when the device already
  happened to be streaming in that direction, so setting the amp gain
  before starting a stream silently did nothing.
- closeStream() now deactivates the stream first.

The first of those is the one behavioural change worth flagging:
automatic baseband-filter selection is gone with it. _auto_bandwidth is
still written but no longer read, so a client that only calls
setSampleRate() no longer gets a filter picked for it, and setBandwidth
now passes the raw request to the firmware (which rounds up) instead of
SoapySDR rounding it down. That is upstream's deliberate fix for the
bandwidth bug, not a regression.
- cmake_minimum_required became the range 2.8.12...3.10, which cmake 4
  accepts on its own. The -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 workaround
  is therefore dropped; verified green against Tumbleweed's cmake 4.4.2
  and Leap 16.0's 3.31.7.

The version format is +git, not ~git: labelCompare(0.3.4,
0.3.4+git20251009.143ff5e) is -1, so the snapshot sorts above the tag;
~git would sort below it and be a downgrade. Same form as Factory's own
soapy-sdr, whose _service this one is modelled on, except that the
revision is pinned to the full sha instead of &quot;master&quot;, so the tarball
is reproducible. The committed tarball is content-identical to GitHub's
archive of that sha.

For the record: Gentoo, NixOS and FreeBSD all still ship the 0.3.4 tag,
so nobody else carries a snapshot. Upstream has not tagged since 2022
and publishes no GitHub releases at all, so waiting for a tag means
waiting indefinitely for fixes that have been on master for four years.

Also carried over from sr#1374754:

Add an explicit Requires: soapy-sdr to the module subpackage. The module
links libSoapySDR, so it has always had the automatic soname dependency
(libSoapySDR.so.0.8-3), and the loader itself - the SoapySDR_loadModules
symbol - lives in that library, so the library was never missing. What
the module never pulled in is the soapy-sdr package, whose only content
is /usr/bin/SoapySDRUtil. This is therefore a usability dependency, not
a functional one: a module with no client on the system is useless,
which is the point raised in review on sr#1374694. The rest of the
SoapySDR plugin family is getting the same treatment.

Plus %cmake_build instead of a bare make call and a copyright header
refresh.</comment>
